2186045585 true] [17592186407240 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}{v}^{2},\\,u-v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2},\\,u-1) \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=u-1,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=t-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThese are parametric equations of a parabolic arc. Notice that if we eliminate $t$ from the equations, we get\n\n$$\nx=(y+1)^{2}\n$$\n\nwhich is a right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,-1).$\n\nMoreover, the endpoints of ${S}_{3}$ are mapped to the $xy$-plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T:(1,1)\\to ({1}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2},\\,1-1)=(1,0) \\\\  & T:(0,1)\\to ({0}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2},\\,0-1)=(0,-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${S}_{3}$ is an arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(0,-1).$\n\n![](images/d8/d8861cf6be2cb40702ec6f97d75dbb55e50cdde32a5152428dcdeecf839f270a.png)" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407235 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1069 "q-225047" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+2v,\\,y=v-2u.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1072 #uuid "5c666819-f94c-5831-9c13-86415b44c537" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407241 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+2v,\\,v-2u) \\\\  & =({0}^{2}+2v,\\,v-2(0)) \\\\  & =(2v,v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2v,\\,y=v,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(2,1)$ and $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/0b/0b61f3a91c912dcd042bdd5cc11b0f393a8ea85269ecbef000403cf080166cf7.png)" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407236 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1069 "q-225018" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v+2u,\\,y=u({v}^{2}-1).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=2t,\\,y=y(t),\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nFind the function $y(t).$" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1072 #uuid "d45fe3c2-157b-597a-b7a4-36ff992f60f4" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true] [17592186407242 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $v=0.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v+2u,\\,u({v}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =(0+2u,\\,u(0-1)) \\\\  & =(2u,-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=-t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$" 13194139533533 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00826534-9ddb-597e-a5b4-4a93def9bd22" 17592186407210 "answer-0f3dd863-4c20-526b-baf8-1dd1aaa12685" 17592186407211 "answer-1402d9d4-6fb9-5711-a369-724d5ea71016" 17592186407212 "answer-2e26268d-49a1-5a83-8429-e2dbae2639b1" 17592186407213 "answer-339db576-bc8c-5b76-9e7a-ca3861bc68aa" 17592186407214 "answer-44ffdafc-3200-56d7-8223-b6163e910bc1" 17592186407215 "answer-4589a8a7-f051-572e-a25b-cba772b96ff3" 17592186407216 "answer-4df51f26-e472-5a52-9d84-60f233e16ec0" 17592186407217 "answer-5165e145-830c-56a0-9173-fcfbf2800e9e" 17592186407218 "answer-524c3a00-a206-5dde-a568-5a05da724097" 17592186407219 "answer-585890c6-349d-5e4b-9e94-a9bab08010cd" 17592186407220 "answer-64581119-0bb0-5b9d-9448-7470ca81dcea" 17592186407221 "answer-87c16c9a-0fa3-5130-8d05-8c94f59b0ee7" 17592186407222 "answer-924df19c-bb6c-5527-89a8-97aeec9e95f7" 17592186407223 "answer-b16f1a1f-9a49-5973-9be2-b7ebcc061568" 17592186407224 "answer-b8c147ca-5893-5b85-a3fd-b0d1b30cb874" 17592186407225 "answer-c2dcac8d-e192-52d2-a860-f232f64707c1" 17592186407226 "answer-ca1c4bec-d2d1-5ebd-aec5-afc647b5dca6" 17592186407227 "answer-d56a8ed2-f8fb-51b4-ad31-de2d59c40721" 17592186407228 "answer-d65a3cae-36d7-5c36-ad61-74f27433b1cf" 17592186407229 "answer-dc27fb6b-147f-5701-a343-70552c33d5c0" 17592186407230 "answer-dc7efbbb-13d6-52d4-bb72-add